From 60cb03efd0724da97e10f88ffd10843e6846809d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): roce proxy and rank0 fast-core affinity
 partition

Partition GB10 Cortex-X925 performance cores into disjoint affinity sets
across sparknet RoCE proxy, VLLM::Worker_TP* main and background threads,
VLLM::EngineCore, and Rank-0 APIServer processes.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d6f491081bd1dcbb70f3205fb0bf8a
Rationale: On GB10, Rank 0 runs APIServer, EngineCore, Worker_TP0 (with
28 background threads), and sparknet-proxy in a shared 10-core pool,
causing preemption and arrival skew across the 116 per-step one-shot RoCE
collectives.
Quality implications: None (deterministic thread scheduling only).
Tests: pytest tests/v1/worker/test_roce_cpu_affinity.py
Upstream status: local experiment.
